        <div class="divider"></div>
        <section id="phase-3" data-reveal>
          <p class="label">Phase 3: GA</p>
          <h2>Close the loop without breaking the flow</h2>
          <p>
            GA added training and AI. Both made the product complete. Both threatened to bury the
            builder.
          </p>

          <h3>Adding a product without adding a step</h3>
          <p>
            Training was its own product, with its own settings, and it had to live inside the builder.
            Three steps were about to become four, and the under-a-minute goal was at risk.
          </p>
          <p>
            With my PM, I pulled three levers: cut scope, reduce steps, and consolidate. I explored five
            ways to navigate the steps before realizing the steps were the problem. I dropped the wizard
            for a single form with a live preview, and made training an optional toggle.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="wide pair" data-reveal>
        <figure>
          <BuilderWireframe />
          <figcaption>Low-fidelity builder</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <BuilderNavVariants />
          <figcaption>Stage navigation variants</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Replaces the MD's header / form / live preview table: the builder shows that layout directly. -->
      <div class="demo-stage" data-reveal>
        <div class="demo-stage-inner">
